## Interface: 16001
## Title: |cffC9A24ATwich|rUI Workshop
## Notes: Browse the recipes of your professions, queue crafts, see the combined materials still needed, and scan auction prices to see which crafts may be worth making. Loaded only when you open it (/tui workshop); keep it turned on alongside TwichUI.
## Author: twichie
## Version: 1.0.0
## RequiredDeps: !!!TwichUI
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## SavedVariables: TwichUIWorkshopDB
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\!!!TwichUI\media\icon
## X-License: MIT (code); see !!!TwichUI\LICENSE
## Category: Interface Enhancements

# Names, limits and small checks (no game calls, no frames); it creates R.Workshop
Data.lua
# Explicit external source; active Workshop recognizes the small delivered header only.
BridgeCodec.lua
BridgeSchema.lua
BridgeValidate.lua
SummarySchema.lua
Prepared.lua
Summary.lua
Bridge.lua
ServerMarket.lua
# The combined materials and what is still needed (pure)
Materials.lua
# The saved queue of the current character (TwichUIDB.workshop; the market data has its own saved variables, TwichUIWorkshopDB)
Queue.lua
# The recipes a character knows, remembered between sessions (TwichUIDB.workshop, per character)
Known.lua
# What the profession window offers: the player's own recipes, their output and materials (game reads only)
Observe.lua
# What the player's bank and the guild bank were last seen to hold (saved in TwichUIDB.workshop.storage; no game calls, no frames)
Storage.lua
# The material-availability service: bags, bank and guild bank kept apart, one allocation for every view (pure)
Stock.lua
# The price history of one item: a compact, bounded string per item (pure)
History.lua
# The price distribution of one item: quartiles, the Recent Price, the saved text and its checked reading (pure)
Dist.lua
# The version-2 history of one item: the 48-hour ring, 30 daily points, weekly and two-week buckets, the append path (pure)
History2.lua
# Auction prices: collecting a scan, the saved markets (TwichUIWorkshopDB), what one craft costs and earns (no game calls, no frames)
Prices.lua
# The Opportunities list: rows, filter, sort, the basis text (pure)
Opportunities.lua
# What vendors were seen to charge, and where they are (saved in TwichUIDB.workshop.vendor; no game calls, no frames)
Vendor.lua
# The shopping list: where to get each missing material, or whether to make it (pure)
Shopping.lua
# The multilevel crafting planner: buy or make every material of the whole chain, combined demand, owned stock once (pure; P1, no window uses it yet)
CraftPlanner.lua
# The crafting strategy: words for the planner's plan, its cooperative jobs and the adapter to the shopping rows (P2; pure, plus a frame timer)
Strategy.lua
# "What's it worth?": vendor, auction and disenchant for one item
Worth.lua
# The "What's it worth?" lines the player chose and their order: the saved layout and the one builder the tooltip and the designer share (pure)
WorthLayout.lua
# The price scan of the open auction house (started only by the player's click)
Scan.lua
# The market data API: current prices, history, quotes, markets (one source for every feature; reads saved data only)
Market.lua
Valuation.lua
# Companion reference pricing with independent local scan fallback
Pricing.lua
# Market figures for display: one cached read and the words of each (A7; pure)
MarketFacts.lua
# Auction house fees for estimates: the cut (assumed or matching the Gold Ledger) and the deposit from the player's own postings
Fees.lua
# The planning estimate of a craft: depth-aware, vendor-aware materials, a competition-based sell price, fees, confidence (pure)
Estimate.lua
# One transient, dependency-aware, cooperatively calculated Opportunities catalog
OpportunityEngine.lua
# A8: competition-based selling suggestions and deterministic item advice
Sell.lua
DisenchantData.lua
DisenchantExclusions.lua
Disenchant.lua
Advisor.lua
# Opening the auction house: when a price update is due, and what to do about it (A6; pure policy plus one entry point)
Auto.lua
# What the window shows and does, without any frame
Session.lua
# A8: item discovery, preferences and the adapter to existing planning services
AdvisorData.lua
# Progress on the plan: the player's "Crafted one"; the game's evidence is off until verified (P2.1)
Progress.lua
# Remembers the player's own professions' recipes while the window is closed (after load only; reads, never opens anything)
Watch.lua
# Remembers the bank and the guild bank while they are open, window hidden or not (after load only; reads, never moves anything)
Bank.lua
# The "What's it worth?" lines on the tooltip of an item in the bags or bank (after load only; reads saved prices, never the auction house)
WorthTip.lua
Junk.lua
# The progress bar and the Scan prices button on the auction house window (the click goes through Session)
AuctionButton.lua
# The window's presentation helpers: the settings window's crafted look through the core's CraftLook.lua (TwichUI_Settings is never loaded)
Style.lua
# Shared interactive market charts for Workshop and Auction House pages
auction/AdvancedChart.lua
# The Gold Ledger: what its page reads (pure) and its Gold Flow chart; the recorder is the core's auction/Ledger.lua (docs/workshop/gold-ledger.md)
# Coin artwork for money in the Ledger (gold, silver and copper icons instead of letters); presentation only
Coins.lua
LedgerQuery.lua
ChartKit.lua
LedgerChart.lua
# The pages, in the order the page list shows them (each builds once and draws what Session.lua says)
ViewOverview.lua
ViewOpportunities.lua
ViewCrafting.lua
ViewShopping.lua
ViewAdvisor.lua
# The full strategy view and the confirmation before an optimized plan is added to the queue (P2)
ViewStrategy.lua
# The Gold Ledger page: gold gained and spent, by day and by source (reads only; the core records)
ViewLedger.lua
# The compact companion: Travel and Craft, a small panel in the window's place (P2.1)
Compact.lua
# Progress notices through TwichUI's notification coordinator (P2.1)
Notice.lua
# Standalone AH presentation preview; no native takeover or transaction actions
auction/Window.lua
auction/Components.lua
auction/ReadRequests.lua
auction/Categories.lua
auction/BrowseData.lua
auction/ViewBrowse.lua
auction/MarketData.lua
auction/ShoppingData.lua
auction/ViewShopping.lua
auction/SellData.lua
auction/Actions.lua
auction/Debug.lua
auction/ViewSell.lua
auction/ViewOwned.lua
auction/ViewMarket.lua
